WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.288 --> 00:00:05.871
(techno music)

00:00:07.445 --> 00:00:10.165
- Today, we are going
to be smiling all day.

00:00:10.165 --> 00:00:11.000
Whatever we're doing,

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.176
we're gonna have a big smile on our face.

00:00:13.176 --> 00:00:15.267
- I don't really think I smile.

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:16.517
I try to avoid it actually.

00:00:16.517 --> 00:00:19.644
- I also smile when I'm
trying to alleviate tension

00:00:19.644 --> 00:00:20.736
or awkwardness.

00:00:20.736 --> 00:00:21.598
- I've learned throughout the years

00:00:21.598 --> 00:00:23.071
that some people are scared to talk to me

00:00:23.071 --> 00:00:24.715
or think that I'm unapproachable.

00:00:24.715 --> 00:00:27.715
I didn't realize that my default face was.

00:00:27.715 --> 00:00:28.976
- I wanna find out if it's true

00:00:28.976 --> 00:00:31.673
that if you smile all the
time it makes you happy.

00:00:31.673 --> 00:00:34.176
Is happiness just a muscle contraction?

00:00:34.176 --> 00:00:35.427
- I think I wear my
emotions on my sleeves.

00:00:35.427 --> 00:00:37.073
If I don't like someone, you'll know,

00:00:37.073 --> 00:00:38.795
but I feel like it's a skill

00:00:38.795 --> 00:00:40.355
not to like someone and still be like,

00:00:40.355 --> 00:00:42.306
"How are you doing?"

00:00:42.306 --> 00:00:44.507
I wanna be able to mask it when I want.

00:00:44.507 --> 00:00:46.787
- I think I'm literally
gonna look like the joker.

00:00:46.787 --> 00:00:48.885
- I'm scared that my smiling
face will look creepy.

00:00:48.885 --> 00:00:53.331
- Also worried that I'm gonna
feel like a big old phony.

00:00:53.331 --> 00:00:55.185
- I'm gonna go sit down at my desk

00:00:55.185 --> 00:00:57.966
and just smile at my computer.

00:00:57.966 --> 00:00:59.799
- Smiling and working.

00:01:01.266 --> 00:01:04.411
Just keep smiling,
smiling, smiling, smile.

00:01:04.411 --> 00:01:05.291
- It's really nice.

00:01:05.291 --> 00:01:06.991
Seeing you happy makes me happy.

00:01:06.991 --> 00:01:07.893
- I walked into the room,

00:01:07.893 --> 00:01:09.371
and I was like, there's something great

00:01:09.371 --> 00:01:11.861
and even more pleasant
than usual about him today.

00:01:11.861 --> 00:01:14.621
- Liz was telling me about how
her dad forgot her birthday.

00:01:14.621 --> 00:01:16.821
Not a funny story, but I
had to smile through it.

00:01:16.821 --> 00:01:18.321
I felt so awkward.

00:01:23.386 --> 00:01:25.167
- It seems more like I
have my life together,

00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:29.039
and I'm just like a happy
person all the time.

00:01:29.039 --> 00:01:30.719
- You know how like
when guys on the street

00:01:30.719 --> 00:01:33.319
tell you to smile, and
you tell them to fuck off,

00:01:33.319 --> 00:01:34.487
I guess they won't do that anymore,

00:01:34.487 --> 00:01:36.269
'cause they have no reason
to tell me to smile,

00:01:36.269 --> 00:01:39.102
'cause I'm already smiling, bitch.

00:01:41.328 --> 00:01:43.239
- It's a hot day in this sweater,

00:01:43.239 --> 00:01:46.780
and I'm just smiling,
like nothing is wrong.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:49.140
- [Armand] Do we look
happier as people right now?

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:50.569
- You look like you're in pain.

00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:52.991
- Yeah, I'm definitely in pain.

00:01:52.991 --> 00:01:55.649
It's really painful to have your lips

00:01:55.649 --> 00:01:57.420
out like this all the time.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:00.087
(playful music)

00:02:02.273 --> 00:02:04.869
- Other than the cramping
that's happening in my face,

00:02:04.869 --> 00:02:07.389
I think it's kind of
effecting the way I feel.

00:02:07.389 --> 00:02:10.980
Convinces me and my body
that I'm having a great time.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.551
- I do feel like I have
a lot of energy though,

00:02:13.551 --> 00:02:14.384
which is weird,

00:02:14.384 --> 00:02:16.959
and I think it's because
I can't relax my face.

00:02:16.959 --> 00:02:18.116
- It's really weird smiling,

00:02:18.116 --> 00:02:19.269
because I'm listening to some

00:02:19.269 --> 00:02:21.819
super angsty emo music right now.

00:02:21.819 --> 00:02:24.551
To properly enjoy my angsty music,

00:02:24.551 --> 00:02:27.721
I have to be brooding,
and I can't do that.

00:02:27.721 --> 00:02:28.554
- In the middle of eating lunch,

00:02:28.554 --> 00:02:30.503
I realized that I lost my phone.

00:02:30.503 --> 00:02:32.611
I'm hoping that it's at the office,

00:02:32.611 --> 00:02:34.223
even though I'm slightly panicking,

00:02:34.223 --> 00:02:36.051
'cause all my credit cards are in there.

00:02:36.051 --> 00:02:38.957
You can't tell, because I am smiling.

00:02:38.957 --> 00:02:42.068
- I'll have a negative
thought about something,

00:02:42.068 --> 00:02:46.567
and then I'll feel my face
kind of melt into a frown,

00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:48.757
and then I'll pick it
back up into a smile.

00:02:48.757 --> 00:02:51.748
It stops me from having
a negative thought.

00:02:51.748 --> 00:02:55.027
- It's like a workout
on my face and my soul.

00:02:55.027 --> 00:02:57.090
(playful music)

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:58.732
- Just finished a meeting
smiling the whole time,

00:02:58.732 --> 00:02:59.844
and the person giving the presentation

00:02:59.844 --> 00:03:02.261
did say I looked creepy, but.

00:03:04.323 --> 00:03:06.364
How's me smiling nonstop?

00:03:06.364 --> 00:03:07.540
- It's a little bit disconcerting,

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.444
because I feel like
usually when people smile

00:03:09.444 --> 00:03:10.833
it's in reaction to something.

00:03:10.833 --> 00:03:12.575
So they're smiling,
because they just saw you,

00:03:12.575 --> 00:03:14.793
or they're smiling because
something made them laugh.

00:03:14.793 --> 00:03:16.431
So it's weird to look over at you,

00:03:16.431 --> 00:03:17.815
and you're already smiling.

00:03:17.815 --> 00:03:20.585
- I'm saying hi to people more often.

00:03:20.585 --> 00:03:21.418
I don't know what it is.

00:03:21.418 --> 00:03:24.513
I think having a big smile might make me

00:03:24.513 --> 00:03:25.873
a little more welcoming.

00:03:25.873 --> 00:03:28.015
- [Kane] Is the way you
perceive me slightly different

00:03:28.015 --> 00:03:30.126
with me smiling?
- Yeah, yeah, completely.

00:03:30.126 --> 00:03:32.084
- Yeah, you just seem like warm.

00:03:32.084 --> 00:03:33.412
- You just like welcoming.

00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:35.890
I saw you smiling, and
then I smiled instantly.

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:37.125
- [Kane] How much more welcoming?

00:03:37.125 --> 00:03:38.874
- 48%.

00:03:38.874 --> 00:03:42.874
- Enough for me to talk
to you, and be like "Hey."

00:03:42.874 --> 00:03:44.549
- Surprising.
- People should smile.

00:03:44.549 --> 00:03:45.382
- I'm surprised.

00:03:45.382 --> 00:03:49.992
- Everybody thinks I'm like
super excited to see them,

00:03:49.992 --> 00:03:52.573
but I'm not, I'm just smiling.

00:03:52.573 --> 00:03:54.813
Nobody actually believes me anymore.

00:03:54.813 --> 00:03:56.442
I tried to say something to somebody,

00:03:56.442 --> 00:03:58.013
and they were like, "Is this a joke?"

00:03:58.013 --> 00:03:58.846
and I was like,

00:03:58.846 --> 00:04:02.596
"No, I'm being completely
serious right now."

00:04:13.496 --> 00:04:16.656
- I'm noticing that all my
interactions with other people

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.325
have been pretty great so far.

00:04:18.325 --> 00:04:21.416
Being a smiley person makes
all of your interactions

00:04:21.416 --> 00:04:23.576
with other human beings very pleasant.

00:04:23.576 --> 00:04:24.993
Who'd have known?

00:04:26.816 --> 00:04:27.757
In like subtle ways,

00:04:27.757 --> 00:04:30.077
it's helped me kind of get out of a slump.

00:04:30.077 --> 00:04:31.995
Next time you're in a
bad mood, try grinning

00:04:31.995 --> 00:04:33.192
and see what happens.

00:04:33.192 --> 00:04:35.824
- Smiling makes other people smile,

00:04:35.824 --> 00:04:37.603
and it makes other people happy.

00:04:37.603 --> 00:04:39.304
It makes you more approachable.

00:04:39.304 --> 00:04:41.203
- I got a lot of mixed
reviews on the smiling.

00:04:41.203 --> 00:04:43.104
Some people thought I
was more approachable.

00:04:43.104 --> 00:04:44.904
Some people though it was creepy.

00:04:44.904 --> 00:04:46.871
Even though I did like
being more approachable,

00:04:46.871 --> 00:04:50.030
at the end of the day, I'd
rather be liked by a few people

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:54.022
but stay real, than by a
ton of people and be fake.

00:04:54.022 --> 00:04:56.605
(upbeat music)

